# Frontend Security Rules

## Related Rules
- @frontend-rules.mdc for general frontend guidelines
- @frontend/core/state-management.mdc for secure state handling
- @frontend/core/testing.mdc for security testing

## Overview
This document defines the rules and best practices for maintaining security in Ruby on Rails frontend applications.

## Security Principles

### 1. CSRF Protection
- Always use Rails CSRF tokens
- Implement proper form authenticity tokens
- Use proper HTTP methods
- Handle CSRF errors gracefully
- Never disable CSRF protection

### 2. XSS Prevention
- Use proper HTML escaping
- Implement Content Security Policy (CSP)
- Sanitize user input
- Use proper Rails view helpers
- Implement proper encoding

### 3. Data Protection
- Never expose sensitive data in views
- Use proper data attributes
- Implement proper access control
- Use proper encryption
- Handle sensitive data securely

## Implementation Guidelines

### CSRF Protection
```ruby
# Good
<%= form_with(model: @user, local: true) do |f| %>
  <%= f.hidden_field :authenticity_token %>
  # ... form fields
<% end %>

# Bad
<%= form_with(model: @user, local: true, skip_csrf: true) do |f| %>
  # ... form fields
<% end %>
```

### XSS Prevention
```ruby
# Good
<%= sanitize @user.bio %>
<%= h @user.name %>

# Bad
<%= raw @user.bio %>
<%= @user.name.html_safe %>
```

## Security Headers
- Implement Content Security Policy
- Use X-Frame-Options
- Use X-XSS-Protection
- Use X-Content-Type-Options
- Use Strict-Transport-Security

## Testing Requirements
- Test CSRF protection
- Test XSS vulnerabilities
- Test data exposure
- Test access control
- Test input validation

## Common Mistakes to Avoid
- Disabling CSRF protection
- Using raw/unsafe HTML
- Exposing sensitive data
- Not implementing proper access control
- Not sanitizing user input
- Not using proper encryption
- Not handling sensitive data securely
- Not implementing proper security headers

## Validation Checklist
- [ ] CSRF protection implemented
- [ ] XSS prevention in place
- [ ] Data protection implemented
- [ ] Security headers configured
- [ ] Tests cover security scenarios
- [ ] Access control implemented
- [ ] Input validation in place
- [ ] Sensitive data handled securely
